+## diff and derive-changes: indexed validation follows comparison and output
+
+Decoded blobs still check block, group and element framing, string-table
+UTF-8, tag indices and dense tag runs, packed IDs, coordinates, refs and
+member arrays, and countable parallel arrays in the element messages.
+Kind, ID-range, count and order claims still pass the existing checks.
+Tags stay fully validated because the packed equality shortcut can decide
+equality without resolving each index. Dense tag run boundaries align the
+tags to node IDs. Refs and members keep their packed checks so an
+incomplete value cannot shorten the sequence used for comparison.
+Coordinate scaling and relation role resolution keep their existing
+comparison and output semantics.
+
+Metadata is checked at the first use of the record or dense group. Text
+checks the versions it prints, including the old version on common lines
+without `-c`. Verbose text adds content details for modified pairs, so
+only the printed versions need metadata. OSC checks visibility on both
+sides when the content is equal, the old version for a delete, and all
+metadata on the new record for a create or modify. Count-only diff
+needs no metadata. Once a dense metadata message is used, its framing
+and all packed columns are checked against the ID count. Full output
+replays the group's deltas from its start, including before a clipped
+window or an unchanged node.
+
+A metadata message with no such use can carry malformed inner framing,
+duplicate packed fields, invalid packed varints or mismatched dense
+metadata column lengths. Its enclosing message still has to be framed
+correctly. For plain Info opened only for version or visibility, field
+framing and the selected scalar are checked. A terminated varint in
+another scalar field can exceed the decoder's value width, since only
+its end is needed to find the selected field. No skipped value can
+contribute to equality or be printed. A used visibility column must
+be checked before it can supply an equality verdict, even when there
+will be no output for that element.
+
+Metadata defects can now be reported after a content or claim defect
+that the same blob also carries, or after earlier records have been
+written to a text stream. The sequential path for inputs without
+indexdata and public block construction retain full validation. The
+existing compressed-byte equality shortcut still skips decoding eligible
+identical blobs.
+
 ## tags-filter and inspect tags: expression-syntax edge cases
 
 The matcher is built to match `osmium-tool/src/util.cpp::get_string_matcher`
